{"term":"observe","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:fdc38c486c6efb4945","definition":"To notice or view, especially carefully or with attention to detail.","example":"From this vantage point we can observe the behavior of the animals in their natural habitat.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["observance","observant","observation","observational","observatory","observer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7136b3c29fd280c918","definition":"To follow or obey the custom, practice, or rules (especially of a religion).","example":"Please observe all posted speed limits.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["celebrate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["observance","observant","observation","observational","observatory","observer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fdc430c5a6f7413d77","definition":"To take note of and celebrate (a holiday or similar occurrence), to keep; to follow (a type of time or calendar reckoning).","example":"Ye shall observe the feast of unleavened bread.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["observance","observant","observation","observational","observatory","observer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e4d8b85cf600fb92b5","definition":"To comment on something; to make an observation.","example":"The senator observed that the bill would be detrimental to his constituents.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["observance","observant","observation","observational","observatory","observer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4e3df7bcb0650948e3","definition":"An observation (remark, comment or judgement).","example":"“It sticks in my mind that he would take it very ill,” says Alan. “But the little man cried to me to run, and indeed I thought it was a good observe, and ran. The last that I saw they were all in a knot upon the beach, like folk that were not agreeing very well together.”","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["observance","observant","observation","observational","observatory","observer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/əbˈzɜːv/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a7/En-us-observe.ogg/En-us-observe.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["observance","observant","observation","observational","observatory","observer"]}